            <ArticleTitle>From acute pain to chronic pain: a personal journal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 1985 I had back surgery, and I began to keep a journal. I thought it would help me track my progress. I wrote in it often, sometimes two or three times a day. It became a lifeline for me. Four years and ten volumes later it tells my story, the story of my struggle with pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
